Directory "no-such-dir" does not exist.

Usage:
    find-covers [options] <inputDir> <outputDir>

    inputDir      the tree whose audio files are looked at; only read.
    outputDir     where what is found is written, at the same relative path:
                  a copy of the file with the cover embedded, or the cover as
                  an image - folder.jpg for an album, one named after the
                  file under -s. Created if missing, and refused if it lies
                  inside inputDir.
Options:
    -h, --help      Print this help page.
    -i, --ignore-folder-covers
                    Also look for a file or album whose folder holds a cover
                    image (folder.jpg, cover.png, an image sharing its name,
                    ...), rather than taking that image as its cover.
    -l, --min-length <minutes>
                    Leave alone a file shorter than this; an album is not
                    held to it, its tracks are under -t. A fraction is
                    allowed. Default 0, every length.
    -m, --min-megapixels <megapixels>
                    A cover smaller than this - embedded, or the image
                    beside the file - is looked to be replaced, and one
                    found smaller than this is not written. A fraction is
                    allowed; 0 keeps and writes any cover. Default 0.25
    -n, --dry-run   Only list the files and albums that would be looked for;
                    nothing is searched or written.
    -s, --sidecar   Write the cover found for a file that is no album track
                    beside it, as an image named after it (track.jpg),
                    rather than embedding it in a copy.
    -t, --per-track Look for an album's tracks one by one, like any other file,
                    rather than for the album once as its folder.jpg.
    -z, --min-size <megabytes>
                    Leave alone a file smaller than this; an album is not
                    held to it, its tracks are under -t. A fraction is
                    allowed. Default 0, every size.
    -A, --ai        Let language models help (docs/models.md). Without -A no
                    step asks one; the commands this one starts are handed it.
    -v, --verbose   Also say why each item was handled the way it was, and on a
                    failure print the tool's whole output rather than its last
                    lines.
    -q, --quiet     Print errors only - no progress and no warnings.
    -x, --set <name=value>
                    Override a setting for this run, over the settings file;
                    repeatable. A secret is refused - the settings file is where
                    it goes. The settings page lists the names.
